{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105461-house-balor-and-the-sevartal","id":1105461,"title":"House Balor and the Sevartal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-19T11:12:21-07:00","id":1105461,"title":"House Balor and the Sevartal","content":"Before C20 introduced Sevartal to us I used to play with the idea that House Balor Sidhe were actually the Sidhe Thallain, or as close to one as the Sidhe could have. This was die to few simple facts of previous editions. Namely that House Balor claimed Fomorian blood ties, and as we all know Thallain are the Fomorians answer to the Kiths, and that one of the main differences, mechanically, between Thallain and Kiths used to be that Thallain had two Unseelie Legacies and thus were always Unseelie and the Sidhe of House Balor were likewise permanently Unseelie even though they still had Legacies of both Courts. It just was so that their Seelie Legacy could never be the dominant one due to their Fomorian blood. This theory was enforced by the fact that we never had a Sidhe equivalent counted with the Thallain.<br /> <br /> Now the Thallain got some nifty new mechanics through Nightmare Legacies, a change I liked as it made them something different form the Unseelie, and new types of Thallain as well like the Sevartal. Now this is all cool and I will likely use them in my Chronicles, perhaps even changing one of my big bad's behind a wast conspiracy to a Sevartal, but it also means that it eats away at some previous reputations and assumptions. Simply put the existence of the Sevartal makes House Balor loose some of it's previous oomph and status. Like in the Chronicle I mentioned previously the NPC I might replace with a Sevartal, an NPC the players have yet to meet, has been until now a Sidhe of House Balor as they were the most suited for a conspiracy of Nightmares that involves other supernaturals as well. Now the Sevartal are more suited for that position. In fact they are quite suited for many positions I would have previously used House Balor for. Anyone else have this problem or is it just me?<br /> <br /> Similarly I liked to think that the reason Redcaps didn't have a Thallain equivalent was that there could be nothing more Nigthmarish than them, now we got Ghasts who are required by their Frailties to be worse than Redcaps, concerning humans atleast, and that eats a bit of the Redcap cake so to speak. Still like with the Sevartal I welcome Ghasts as they do bring interesting opportunities.<br /> <br /> But now back to the Sevartal.<br /> Now that we have them we seriously need some Thallain Houses. If they are to be the twisted reflections of the Sidhe they need Houses of their own.<br /> <br /> Also I must not be the only who noticed that they are described in a way that makes them the obvious Fae behind the Kiasyd Bloodline of Vampires. I used to theorize that the dark alchemy that changed Marconius had to have Sidhe blood involved in it somehow as they were the only Kith the Kiasyd remotely resembled but now we have the Sevartal who like the Kiasyd softly glow bluish in the moonlight and are lithe and tall like the Sidhe and bearing pointed ears. Also of hte Fae touched vampires only the Kiasyd can Embrace others who become just likethemselves, with all the same features, just like the Sevartal can twist the other Fae into their likeness.<br /> <br /> As a final thought why does House Balor have the Flaw that restricts their Willpower? Mostly I ask because after reading their entry in the Book of Houses 2 one does not leave with an impression of a weak willed House. And is not their Challenge of a physical deformity be enough? Considering their House Boon, strong as it is, is only of use in the Autum World. They gain no edge of any kind within the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts, hopefully to inspire conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:22:07-07:00","id":1105466,"title":"","content":"How did you hand non-sidhe members of House Balor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:40:52-07:00","id":1105471,"title":"","content":"Perhaps while in the Dreaming, House Balor might gain some advantageous mutation ala Demonic Investment? Perhaps this could be based on the Balor's Rank and thematically linked with his or her deformity.<br /> <br /> Armor (varies)<br /> Every point invested in Armor grants the fae an additional soak die against damage.<br /> <br /> Beast Form (3 pts)<br /> The fae can shape-shift into a beast.<br /> <br /> Claws or horns (varies)<br /> For one point the fae sprouts claws or horns which do aggravated damage. For an additional point the claws or horns are made retractable.<br /> <br /> Demonic Strength (varies)<br /> For every three points the fae can increase his Strength or Stamina by one.<br /> <br /> Devil's Eyes (2 pts)<br /> With a glance the fae can spoil milk, rot plants, and sicken children.<br /> <br /> Goat Feet (2 pts)<br /> The fae's feet change into goat's hooves from sundown to sunrise.<br /> <br /> Hellfire (3 pts)<br /> The fae can breathe Hellfire on her victims (3 dice of aggravated damage).<br /> <br /> Invulnerability (3 pts)<br /> For every 3 points invested in this power the fae gains one soak die against all attacks.<br /> <br /> Regeneration (9 pts)<br /> The fae can heal wounds by spending 1 Willpower point for every Health Level to be healed.<br /> <br /> Serpent Skin (3 pts)<br /> The fae can literally shed her skin to escape her bonds.<br /> <br /> Shameful Sight (6 pts)<br /> By gazing into a victim's eyes the fae can determine the victim's greatest sin.<br /> <br /> Sign of Inferno / Hell Skinned (5 pts)<br /> The fae becomes immune to normal fires.<br /> <br /> Talons of the Plague-Crow (8 pts)<br /> The fae sprouts talons that cause severe illness in those struck by them.<br /> <br /> Wings (3 pts)<br /> The Infernalist can grow large, horrible wings to grant her temporary flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-19-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T14:29:57-07:00","id":1105516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105461-house-balor-and-the-sevartal?p=1105466#post1105466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you hand non-sidhe members of House Balor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite sure what you mean, but this is handled by the Book of Houses 2 where there is a seperate Oath taken by non-Sidhe who are adobted to the House. Let's just say it involves self-mutilation.<br /> <br /> If you mean how does their existence affect the thematic space I, obviously erranously, assumed the House to occupy as a dark reflection of the other Houses. In my opinion it didn't affect it at all. At the point where you voluntarily subject yourself to self-mutilation to join them you are already aware of the kind of people your associating with and eager to further their goals.<br /> <br /> Again this brings is back to the question of why do Balor bear two, before it was three, challenges, or flaws, where other Houses generally bear just one. They bear a physical, for the Sidhe magical in nature, deformity, and are restricted to willpower 6. As said they do gain a considerable boon for it, which was slightly boosted in C20, but that boon does absolutely nothing in the Dreaming, which is a design flaw in my opinion considering that the House not only spends considerable amount of time in the Dreaming, they consider themselves hunters of dangerous chimera and guardians of silver paths and have a faction dedicated to this. And their part of the Book of Houses did not read to me at any point as being weak of will. It's just an odd flaw with an odd excuse of being there due to the wild influence of Fomorian Blood but the closest beings to Fomorians that we have rules for are the Thallain and they have no limits to their willpower. I can handle the weakness being there ofcourse but I just dont get the reason it is there.<br /> <br /> @MythAdvocate<br /> That is actually a good idea for a house rule. Though one that can easily get out of hand or seem too powerful. These could also be handled by merits only described accordingly for the deformity. Also commoner Kiths adobted to the House should in this case manifest as brutal looking growths tied to their mutilations.<br /> <br /> But still those are house rule territory.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else feel Balor lost a little bit of itself as the Sevartal game along? Or is it all just in my head?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T14:58:06-07:00","id":1105520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105461-house-balor-and-the-sevartal?p=1105516#post1105516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MythAdvocate<br /> That is actually a good idea for a house rule. Though one that can easily get out of hand or seem too powerful. These could also be handled by merits only described accordingly for the deformity. Also commoner Kiths adobted to the House should in this case manifest as brutal looking growths tied to their mutilations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be abused, but not by much. Those powers are not any more powerful than a Birthright or Rede.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T15:07:59-07:00","id":1105523,"title":"","content":"Now that I think of it, I don't like Thallain all that much. I'd rather convert some of their Kiths I like into Adhene (leaving the most redundant out) and add some Thallain Houses instead (Of which Balor is also one of). For Commoners and Sidhe alike.<br /> <br /> Kithain and Adhene can opt to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-19-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T19:17:07-07:00","id":1105572,"title":"","content":"Here is a thread I made discussing this very topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098714-thallain-houses-house-questions-gallain-nobles-ect-questions\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098714-thallain-houses-house-questions-gallain-nobles-ect-questions\"> Thallain Houses, House Questions, Gallain/Nobles ect Questions... - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098714-thallain-houses-house-questions-gallain-nobles-ect-questions\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098714-thallain-houses-house-questions-gallain-nobles-ect-questions </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So shouldn't the Thallain have some houses? Now that they finally have a Noble Thallain, the Sevartal, well and the Merrow count as well... Do some of the Thallain join House Balor or other Houses? What about the Merrow why don't they have a house when the Merfolk all have houses? And shouldn't the Oba at least have one house of their own if not more since they are a whole kith founded outside the European Dreaming? Shouldn't they have something like a House Chango, House Eshu, ect? For the Thallain I like to think they have more worldwide cultures for their house rather then the Western Europe </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}